.Dd December 4, 2014
.Dt XOHTML 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xohtml
.Nd display libxo html output
.Xr xo_emit 3
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm xohtml
.Op Fl b Ar base
.Op Fl c Ar command
.Op Fl f Ar output
.Op Fl k
.Op Fl l
.Op Ar command Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a tool for preparing
.Xr libxo 3
HTML output for display in modern HTML web browsers.
.Nm
can operate in two modes.
If command is provided
either with the
.Fl c
option or as argument(s) to the
.Nm
command, that command is executed and the resulting output is processed.
If no command is given, the
standard input is used.
.Pp
.Nm
is typically used to wrap
.Nm libxo
output with sufficient HTML content to allow display in a web browser.
This includes parent HTML tags, a CSS stylesheet, and an inlined
Javascript tooltip.
.Pp
If the command is given directly on the command line,
.Nm
will add the "--libxo=html" option needed to generate HTML output
from
.Nm libxo Ns
-enabled applications.
See
.Xr xo_options 7
for details.
.Pp
Unless
.Fl f
is given,
.Nm
writes its output to an automatically named file under
.Pa /tmp/$USER.xohtml
and opens it in a browser
(using
.Xr open 1
or
.Xr xdg-open 1 ,
whichever is available).
On each run,
.Nm
also removes stale files left behind by earlier runs from that
directory, unless they were saved with
.Fl k .
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl b Ar base | Fl -base Ar base
Supplies a source path for the CSS stylesheet referenced in
the output of
.Nm xohtml .
Overrides both the default and
.Fl l .
.It Fl c Ar command | Fl -command Ar command
Use the given command instead of one on the command line.
This command should be quoted if it consists of multiple tokens, and
should contain the "--libxo=html" option or equivalent, since the
command is used directly.
.It Fl f Ar file | Fl -file Ar file
Output is saved to the given file, rather than to an automatically
named file, and no browser is opened.
.It Fl k | Fl -keep
Saves the generated file under a name that
.Nm Ns 's
own cleanup pass will not remove on a later run.
Only meaningful when
.Fl f
is not given.
.It Fl l | Fl -local
Uses the installed local copy of the CSS stylesheet, instead of
fetching it from the official
.Nm libxo
website, which is the default source.
.El
.Pp
.Sh EXAMPLES
The following command line will run "du --libxo=html ~/src", write the
result to an automatically named file under /tmp, and open it in a
browser:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
    xohtml du ~/src
.Ed
.Pp
The following command line will run "du --libxo=html ~/src" and save
the output to /tmp/src.html without opening a browser:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
    xohtml du ~/src -f /tmp/src.html
.Ed
.Pp
The following command line will run "du --libxo=html,warn ~/src" and save
the output to /tmp/src.html:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
    du --libxo=html,warn ~/src | xohtml -f /tmp/src.html
.Ed
.Pp
The following command line will run "du --libxo=html,warn ~/src" and save
the output to /tmp/src.html:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
    xohtml -c "du --libxo=html,warn ~/src" -f /tmp/src.html
.Ed
.Pp
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libxo 3 ,
.Xr xo_emit 3 ,
.Xr xo_options 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm libxo
library first appeared in
.Fx 11.0 .
